<!--
  BlockML Core — bootstrap documentation

  FQN: org.blockml.bml.documentation.BootstrapModel
-->
<block
  xmlns="http://blockml.org/schema/block"
  xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
  xsi:schemaLocation="http://blockml.org/schema/block https://blockml.org/schemas/core/block.xsd
                      "
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:doc="org.blockml.bml.documentation">

  <idea>README.bml, Bootstrap, readFirst, and interpretation context.</idea>

  <documentation>
    Self-hosting bootstrap: the compiler loads framework BML from @blockml/core (and domain
    packages) before user content — TypeRegistry bootstrap, not special-cased type semantics
    in code.

    Bootstrap order (summary):
    1. Core branches — Block, ValueType, Language, Status, Constraint, Capability, Definition
    2. Concrete types — Integer, Decimal, languages, services, constraints
    3. BlockLibrary — library descriptor base (bootstrap, _dependencies, _subLibraries, _schemas, _blocks)
    4. org.blockml.bml.Library — published catalog via _blocks; bootstrap → README
    5. Domain framework BML (e.g. com.machineblocks.bml.core.*)

    README.bml blocks inherit from org.blockml.bml.core.Bootstrap. Library.bml declares the
    library entry point via the bootstrap aggregation (typically &lt;blockml:README /&gt;).
    README blocks serve as library entry points for humans and LLMs — not as composable domain
    types. The readFirst aggregation lists Documentation block instances in mental learning
    order; read these before exploring the rest of the library catalog.

    Interpretation context:
    • Framework BML defines what types ARE — TypeRegistry SSOT
    • Renderers interpret what types MEAN for their target — free manifestation
    • README + readFirst establish shared vocabulary before diving into definitions
    • After the first ten bootstrap documentation blocks, most of the core library can be
      derived directly from Block definitions themselves

    Each registered BlockDefinition from bootstrap is an immutable BomDocument parse result.
  </documentation>

  <references>
    <see file="16_framework_base_types.md">
      Bootstrap Order — framework BML load sequence for TypeRegistry.
    </see>
    <see file="13_bml_to_bom_mapping.md">
      TypeRegistry bootstrap — BML registration algorithm.
    </see>
    <see file="14_compiler_runtime.md">
      CLI bootstrap — loading framework BML before user projects.
    </see>
    <see file="01_system.md">
      Self-hosting bootstrap and BML self-description roadmap (V1/V2/V3).
    </see>
    <see block="core:BlockLibrary">
      Library descriptor base — bootstrap aggregation links to README.
    </see>
    <see block="core:Bootstrap">
      Abstract base for README blocks with readFirst aggregation.
    </see>
    <see block="core:Documentation">
      Base type for entries in readFirst documentation lists.
    </see>
    <see block="doc:Introduction">
      First readFirst entry — BlockML goals and overview.
    </see>
    <see block="doc:ModelingGuidelines">
      Next reading step — recommended patterns for modeling Blocks.
    </see>
  </references>

  <name>BootstrapModel</name>
  <type>doc:BootstrapModel</type>
  <baseType>core:Documentation</baseType>

</block>
